Rule 19(d)(i) prohibits altering to port for a radar contact forward of the beam to avoid a close-quarters situation because doing so could place the vessel in a more dangerous position relative to the other vessel. Specifically, the rule states:

(i) an alteration of course to port, for a vessel forward of the beam, other than for a vessel being overtaken;

This prohibition is aimed at reducing the risk of collision by avoiding maneuvers that might lead to a more hazardous situation. The rationale behind this is that altering course to port for a forward-of-the-beam contact could potentially bring the two vessels closer together or create a more difficult situation to resolve, especially given the limitations and uncertainties associated with radar detection in restricted visibility conditions.
